id=ecarx_e02_ihu717p_bt
name=IHU717P BLE/Classic Bluetooth support
version=2026.07.28.1
versionCode=20260730
author=Dmitry Nearlyny
description=Bluetooth support for ECARX E02 / IHU717P based Geely and Knewstar head units at the stock app path: A2DP Sink, HFP HF Client, PBAP Client, AVRCP Controller with working track metadata and physical media buttons (native libbluetooth.so AVRCP feature-negotiation fix), CarPlay/GOC watchdog. Force-connects A2DP Sink for phones that advertise A2DP but never offer a "Media audio" toggle (e.g. Samsung Galaxy) - without it those phones stay call-only. Fixes missing AVRCP track metadata on iOS: a GetCapabilities race (AVRCP comes up before A2DP, the request times out and AOSP never retries) left RegisterNotification unsent, so no track info ever arrived - patched in libbluetooth.so. Payload slimmed by 13 files (3.8 MB): donor audio-HAL leftovers and the global libchrome/libbase overlays are gone, so the module no longer shadows system-wide libraries. Ignores AVRCP absolute-volume commands from the phone (stock head-unit behaviour): iOS was syncing its ringer volume on notification arrival, which drove head-unit volume to maximum and left music playing at full blast. NOTE: the stock NSMedia media app pauses Bluetooth unless the head-unit source is set to Bluetooth - select Bluetooth as the source (see README).
